{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EdgeBreadthFirstSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each source is discovered first. Then, for each vertex in the order discovered, its out-edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are reported as tree edges (to an undiscovered vertex, which is then discovered) or non-tree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges (to a discovered one); then the vertex is finished. In a directed graph every out-edge of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an explored vertex is reported. In an undirected graph each edge is reported once, from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"end whose edges are examined first: the tree edge is not reported again from the vertex it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"discovered, but a parallel edge to the parent is a non-tree edge, and a self-loop is one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"non-tree edge."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Enumeration-Ca